 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to a report by the department of transportation on noise abatement procedures at certain heliports and airports",
    "basePrintNo": "S7701",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7701-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Transportation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7701\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to a report by the department of transportation on\nnoise abatement procedures at certain heliports and airports\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill authorizes and directs the department of transportation To\nprepare a report on noise abatement procedures at certain heliports\nAnd airports in the county of Suffolk.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1- The New York State department of transportation directed To\nsubmit a report on accordance with the provisions of subdivision 14-a\nof section 14 of the transportation law.  Section 2- Contains\nEffective Date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIncrease demand for helicopter services to the eastern end of Long\nIsland has had an impact on noise levels in local East End\ncommunities, affecting the quality of life of residents living in\nthese communities. Noise abatement procedures depend upon voluntary\ncompliance by aircraft. The purpose of this legislation is to provide\nadditional oversight to the monitoring of, and better compliance with,\nnoise abatement procedures by aircraft flying over the eastern end of\nLong Island.  This, in turn, will help to improve residents' quality\nof life.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take immediately.\n",
